<title>JAPAN: Teijin to acquire U.S. plastic film firm.</title>
<headline>Teijin to acquire U.S. plastic film firm.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teijin Ltd said on Wednesday it had agreed to acquire 667,000 shares of California-based Southwall Technologies Inc for $5 million.</p>
<p>The major Japanese synthetic fibre maker will complete the acquisition of the 8.7 percent stake in the U.S plastic film processing company this month, a Teijin spokesman said.</p>
<p>Southwall Technologies has advanced technology for producing special films such as ultra violet ray-resistant film and electromagnetic wave-proof film, the spokesman said.</p>
